{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>How long will you refuse to humble yourself before.</b> What the Holy One, blessed be He, demands of man is humility and lowliness, and this is the word of the prophet (Isaiah 66:2): ״ואל זה אביט אל עני ונכה רוח וחרד על דברי״ — 'and to this one I look: to the poor and contrite of spirit, who trembles at My word'; and it says (ibid.): ״השמים כסאי והארץ הדום רגלי״ — 'the heavens are My throne and the earth is My footstool' — and they cannot contain Me, in the manner of what is said (I Kings 8:27): ״הנה השמים ושמי השמים לא יכלכלוך אף כי הבית הזה אשר בניתי״ — 'behold, the heavens and the heavens of heavens cannot contain You; how much less this house that I have built' — and if so, what house could you build for Me, and what place could be worthy of Me? And yet, 'I look to the poor and contrite of spirit, and to the one who trembles at My word.' The 'poor' (עני) is the humble one, as it is written (Psalms 51:19): ״לב נשבר ונדכה״ — 'a broken and contrite heart'; and therefore Onkelos, of blessed memory, translated it לאתכנעה — 'to humble oneself.'" "<b>Behold.</b> The weightiness of the plagues upon Pharaoh was because of the weightiness of his heart, for what it says, ״אני הכבדתי את לבו״ — 'I have hardened his heart' — they explained as: He adds weight to his heaviness, because it says above: ״ויוסף לחטא ויכבד לבו הוא ועבדיו״ — 'he continued to sin, and his heart and his servants' hearts grew heavy.' And you already know that Ahab king of Israel, who was a wicked idolater, humbled himself, and his humility availed him, as it is written (I Kings 21:29): ״הראית כי נכנע אחאב מלפני יען כי נכנע מפני לא אביא הרעה בימיו בימי בנו אביא הרעה על ביתו״ — 'Have you seen how Ahab has humbled himself before Me? Because he humbled himself before Me, I will not bring the evil in his days; in his son's days I will bring the evil upon his house.' Nebuchadnezzar the wicked, who did not humble himself — you already know his punishment, that the Holy One, blessed be He, brought him low and banished him from his kingdom. And because he was arrogant and made himself a god, exalting himself and ascending from a human level to a divine level, therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, brought him low, abasing him from a human level to the level of beasts, and he ate grass for seven years like a lowly beast. And his punishment was measure for measure, for the punishment of arrogance is humility and abasement, as it is said (Proverbs 16:18): ״לפני שבר גאון״ — 'before destruction comes pride.' So too Pharaoh the wicked refused to humble himself in his pride and arrogance, and therefore he perished in the end."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:29.387410262Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}